-41"}]},{"heading":"How the case got here","paragraphs":["The Supreme Court heard oral argument in this case on January 13, 2014."],"sources":[{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 3, lines 7-17","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2013/12-1281_pm02.pdf","page_label":"file page 3, lines 7-17"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 86, lines 35-49","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2013/12-1281_pm02.pdf","page_label":"file page 86, lines 35-49"}]},{"heading":"What each side wants","paragraphs":["The Board wants the Court to uphold the President's recess appointments.","the opposing side wants the Court to invalidate those appointments."],"sources":[{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 3, lines 19-47","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2013/12-1281_pm02.pdf","page_label":"file page 3, lines 19-47"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 41, lines 11-31","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2013/12-1281_pm02.pdf","page_label":"file page 41, lines 11-31"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 55, lines 9-15","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2013/12-1281_pm02.pdf","page_label":"file page 55, lines 9-15"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 67, lines 31-43","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2013/12-1281_pm02.pdf","page_label":"file page 67, lines 31-43"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 79, lines 51-41","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2013/12-1281_pm02.pdf","page_label":"file page 79, lines 51-41"}]},{"heading":"What each side says","paragraphs":["The Board argues that historical practice supports broad presidential appointment power.","the opposing side argues that the Senate controls its own recess status."],"sources":[{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 3, lines 19-47","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2013/12-1281_pm02.pdf","page_label":"file page 3, lines 19-47"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 41, lines 11-31","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2013/12-1281_pm02.pdf","page_label":"file page 41, lines 11-31"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 55, lines 9-15","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2013/12-1281_pm02.pdf","page_label":"file page 55, lines 9-15"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 67, lines 31-43","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2013/12-1281_pm02.pdf","page_label":"file page 67, lines 31-43"},{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 79, lines 51-41","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2013/12-1281_pm02.pdf","page_label":"file page 79, lines 51-41"}]},{"heading":"What the justices asked","paragraphs":["Chief Justice Roberts asked if the opposing side would invalidate past appointments.","Justice Scalia asked if practice overrides clear constitutional text."],"sources":[{"evidence_type":"Transcript","label":"Official Supreme Court Transcript — file page 3, lines 49-7","official_url":"https://www.supremecourt.gov/oral_arguments/argument_transcripts/2013/12-1281_pm02.pdf","page_label":"file page 3, line